#X text 240 98 The object treats the specified array as a circular
(ring) buffer for audio signals. The signal on the first (left) audio
inlet is written into the array at the current write position \, while
the signal on the second audio inlet controls the read offset (delay)
relative to the write position and is output through the audio outlet.
The @on property enables or disables writing \, when writing is off
\, the array keeps its contents and only reading is performed.;
